      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "1. **Constructing the Equation:**\n   - Given the remainders of the four integers when divided by $11$, let's denote the four positive integers as $4r+2$, $5r+4$, $6r+6$, and $7r+8$.\n   - The sum of these four numbers can be expressed as:\n     \\[\n     (4r+2) + (5r+4) + (6r+6) + (7r+8)\n     \\]\n\n2. **Simplifying the Sum:**\n   - Combine like terms to simplify the expression:\n     \\[\n     (4r + 5r + 6r + 7r) + (2 + 4 + 6 + 8)\n     \\]\n   - This simplifies to:\n     \\[\n     22r + 20\n     \\]\n\n3. **Finding the Remainder:**\n   - To find the remainder of the sum of the four integers when divided by $11$, we need to evaluate the expression $22r + 20$ modulo $11$.\n   - Since $22r\\) modulo $11$ is equivalent to $0$ (as $22$ is divisible by $11$):\n     \\[\n     22r \\equiv 0 \\pmod{11}\n     \\]\n   - Thus, the expression becomes:\n     \\[\n     0 + 20 \\equiv 20 \\pmod{11}\n     \\]\n\n4. **Finding the Remainder of $20$:**\n   - Now, we need to find the remainder when $20$ is divided by $11$:\n     \\[\n     20 \\div 11 = 1 \\text{ with a remainder of } 9\n     \\]\n     - Therefore, $20 \\equiv 9 \\pmod{11}$.\n\n5. **Conclusion:**\n   - The remainder when the sum of the integers is divided by $11$ is $9$.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{9}\n\\]",
